# Build-context exclusions for the production image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` after the manifest-only install layer,
# so *everything* not listed here rides into the image. Two classes of
# thing must never make that trip:
#
#   1. Secrets. A repo-root `.env` holding an ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (the
#      testbed's deep-loop runners read one) would otherwise be baked
#      into an image layer — readable by anyone who can pull it, and
#      recoverable from the layer history even if a later step deleted
#      it. The production entrypoint no longer autoloads `.env` either
#      (see `packages/server/package.json`, the `prod` script): env in
#      production comes from the host (`fly secrets`, `docker run -e`,
#      systemd), never from a file in the build context.
#
#   2. Host-shaped or bulky state that the image must not inherit:
#      `node_modules/` built against the developer's platform (the
#      image runs its own `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, and an
#      alpine container inheriting a darwin esbuild binary crash-loops
#      exactly the way the dev-minor esbuild bump did), stale `dist/`
#      output that would shadow a fresh `pnpm -r build`, the `.git`
#      history, and the ~11 MB of checked-in model cassettes that only
#      the testbed replays.
#
# CI builds from a clean checkout and so never carried the secret; a
# `docker build` or `fly deploy` from a working tree does. This file is
# what makes the two contexts equivalent.

# Secrets and local env
.env
.env.*
*.local

# VCS and tooling state
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Build output and dependency trees (the image builds its own)
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage
**/coverage
.vite

# Test fixtures — model cassettes the testbed replays; not runtime input
packages/*/test/fixtures

# Docs and repo furniture that no runtime code path reads
docs
*.md
!README.md
LICENSE
LICENSE-DATA
fly.toml

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
